The expansion of E-commerce gave birth to the Indian company Flipkart, where people like you and me can sell and buy. However, what many people don’t know is the fact that you can make money on Flipkart not just by selling, but also through the Flipkart affiliate program.
However, there are two prerequisites before you can commit to any kind of affiliate marketing.
Patience to wait for your website/blog traffic to build and contribute towards your commissions
That’s when you give them the link to the product on Flipkart and that might lead to a purchase on Flipkart.
We know what’s in it for Flipkart and Amazon. The next question you should be asking is, what’s in it for you?
Now that the viewer has made a purchase, it is visible that Flipkart has made some money off of it. However, since the viewer purchases the product after coming from your blog, Flipkart will give you a specific commission.
There are different Flipkart affiliate commission rates for different products,
Large Sports, Fitness Equipment’s, Bicycles, Exercise, Food & Nutrition(Non-Grocery) 5%
Fashion & Lifestyle Categories (Bags, Wallets & Belts, Clothing, Eyewear, Footwear , Kids Accessories, Sunglasses, Watches, Men’s Clothing, Women’s Clothing, Kids’ Clothing, Women’s Footwear, Kids’ & Infant Footwear, Men’s Footwear, Women Ethnic Wear, Women Western Wear, Women Lingerie, Sleep & Swimwear, Women Sports & Gym Wear, Women Accessories, Maternity Wear, Men Accessories & Artificial Jewellery) 4%
Small Home Appliances 4%
If a new customer purchases that product from Flipkart through your website, then you will receive a 10% commission. If it is an existing customer that orders the product, you will still receive a 10% commission.
New customer order v/s existing customer order.
Another important aspect is whether the sale is from a new customer or an existing customer.
Search and select the product: Let’s say you have a blog about handwork sarees. After you’ve described the beauty of their drape and how they were used by royalty in India, providing your viewer with a link immediately increases the probability of them buying a handwork saree.
Copy/paste the code into your website/blog: Once you have generated the code, all you need to do is stick it in your website, and you are good to go!
Promotional banners and widgets: This is a dynamic piece of code that can provide up to date information about the product. These too are customizable and are far more engaging and interactive to viewers.
Search tools: This allows viewers of your website/blog/app to scroll and search on Flipkart while still being active with your content. This makes it easier for them to choose what they like while sticking to the theme of what you have provided.
The best part of Flipkart’s affiliate program is that it is free. Here you have a chance of making money through affiliate marketing without any initial investment.
What are some essential things to keep in mind while being an affiliate marketer on Flipkart?
The user must add the item to his or her shopping cart within one session after clicking on your link, i.e., within 30 minutes of clicking on your link. If the user views your blog and clicks on your link at 4:30 PM, then you will receive a commission only if the user adds that item to his or her shopping cart by 5:00 PM.
How can my blog convince audiences to make purchases on Flipkart?
Step 1: Identify the kind of content that you produce, and the kind of products that go with that content
Tell your readers the truth, not only the advantages but the disadvantages too. This will make them feel that you’ve done your homework and know what you are endorsing, which will, in turn, make you appear more trustworthy.
Give reasons as to what a particular product is offering, its advantages, disadvantages, price, warranty, cost of maintenance, and other such details. Make it one of the best available in today’s market.
Let’s apply these rules in the following passage. Let’s say our blog is about a new baby toy that looks like a cell phone and reads out the number of the digit on the keypad that the baby presses.
(Here, you are appealing to an issue the reader is facing)
Further, it aids them in learning how to count, which is a bonus. The only con is how we might have to change the batteries now and then, but it seems to be a great product!
The baby will not only enjoy the sounds the phone makes but will also help them learn how to count. It will engage them for hours together and encourage interactive learning.
What makes the Flipkart affiliate program different from others?
Amazon provides reports on every transaction. Flipkart, on the other hand, does not offer any daily transaction reports.
Toys & Baby Products | Home | Kitchen Appliances | Kitchen & Housewares 9%
Jewellery (Excluding silver & Gold coins) | Car, Motorbike, Industrial & Scientific Products | Musical Instruments 8%
Televisions | Computers |Consumer Electronics & Accessories (excl. Data Storage Devices) | Mobile Accessories 4%
Data Storage Devices 2%
All Other Categories (Furniture| Kindle devices & E-books| Fire TV stick & other Amazon devices | Others 10%
While both programs help bloggers naturally monetize their content, it seems to be that the plans are suitable for different kinds of people. Developers with a primarily Indian audience, who are new to blogging or digital marketing will be better off with the Flipkart affiliate program.
I can’t say this enough, but consistency is key. Don’t lose hope and work hard on your website, and watch the handsome earnings come your way!
There are so many other great programs out there. Check this video out for Amazon associates instead of getting disheartened about the Flipkart program!
