(Recap: Myanmar | The National Unity Government that succeeded Aung San Suu Kyi announced: making Tether the official currency ）
root According to the Nihon Keizai ShimbunReport, The National Unity Government (NUG, with Aung San Suu Kyi as the State Counselor, currently defined as an illegal organization by the military government), which is opposed to the military government of Myanmar, announced that it will support the issuance of the stable currency USDT in Myanmar to resist the dictatorial military It is possible for the government to control the coinage and then control the people of the whole country.
The NUG was established in April 2020 by members of the pro-democracy parliament, but its election seats in the same year were cancelled by the military government. The NUG's resistance is partly political and partly armed, but generally not enough to regain control of the country However, it still has strong popular support.
Last year, an anonymous project, the Myanmar Kyat (MYD), emerged, trying to give Myanmar citizens the freedom of assets without using a centralized currency system, and intends to issue MYD against Myanmar fiat currency, of which 55% will be distributed to the people and 45% will be distributed To NUG and charities.
As a result, NUG turned to support USDT. The organization began selling “Spring Revolution Special Bonds” in November last year to obtain working capital, and raised $11 million in the first 24 hours to avoid the junta’s restraint .
