Due to the difference in the electrical load of the liquid-cooled transformer between winter and summer, the voltage of the liquid-cooled transformer is slightly different. To meet the voltage requirements, some rural electricians adjust the tap switch at will without performing related tests, resulting in a liquid-cooled transformer split.
If the quality of the arrester is unqualified or is not replaced in time, the liquid-cooled transformer is easily damaged by lightning. During the thunderstorm season each year, the arrester should be sent to the repair and test department to be installed in time after passing the test, and the use of unqualified products is prohibited.
It is strictly forbidden to use the wire itself as the nose of the liquid-cooled transformer and directly connect it to the low-voltage pile head of the distribution transformer. Regularly check and strengthen the connection between the lead and the liquid-cooled transformer pile head to prevent the liquid-cooled transformer from being burnt out due to loosening.
