Bluetooth technology was originally created by the telecommunications giant Ericsson, and the name came from the nickname of a Danish king Harald Bluetooth. Today, Bluetooth wireless technology is the most widely used wireless connection technology on mobile devices.
The operating frequency of Bluetooth is between 2.402GHz and 2.480GHz, and this frequency causes a phenomenon that it easily affects the surrounding radio equipment with similar frequencies. This requires an explanation of the concept of 2.4G wireless technology.
2.4G wireless connection can be used for industrial data transmission, wireless remote control, wireless mouse, wireless keyboard, wireless electronic tag, remote control toy, 2.4g wireless amplifier, wireless microphone, wireless speaker, etc. However, due to technical reasons, 2.4G products must be equipped with a receiver.
