Meaning is a feeling that life is of significance and worthwhile.
This process is often related to connection with something beyond ourselves. * Meaning and purpose are integral to spirituality.
As the peak body for spiritual care and ageing, we know it can come as quite a surprise to many people to find out that spirituality is more than religion.
It is about our sources of meaning and hope, which in turn is intimately related to our connectedness to ourselves, to others and to the world.
It’s about what gets you out of bed in the morning.
Some people have a sense of ultimate purpose that comes from their faith.
Ask yourself these questions:
(meeting with friends, volunteering, fighting for a cause, creating…)
(English poetry, a 1986 tennis tournament, my child died…)
(family dinners, watering the garden, prayer…)
What gives Betty purpose
Betty has always been involved in her local community.
She could see how hard it was for people coming in so Betty makes sure she connects with them and introduces them to others.
“Now that I am older, I can see two sides to every question”.
